{"name":"Bull Shot","hex":"#75442b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bull","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An adult male, specifically:\n An adult male of domesticated cattle or oxen.","An adult male of domesticated cattle or oxen."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Large and strong, like a bull.","Of large mammals, adult male."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bull"},{"term":"shot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tired, weary.","Discharged, cleared, or rid of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of shoot"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bloody Mary (cocktail)","blocks":[{"text":"A Bloody Mary is a cocktail containing vodka, tomato juice, and other spices and flavorings including Worcestershire sauce, hot sauces, garlic, herbs, horseradish, celery, olives, pickled vegetables, salt, black pepper, lemon juice, lime juice and celery salt. Some versions of the drink, such as the \"surf 'n' turf\" Bloody Mary, include shrimp and bacon as garnishes. In the United States, it is usually consumed in the morning or early afternoon, and is popular as a hangover cure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Bloody_Mary_Coctail_with_celery_stalk_-_Evan_Swigart.jpg/330px-Bloody_Mary_Coctail_with_celery_stalk_-_Evan_Swigart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloody_Mary_(cocktail)","wikidata":"Q207711"},{"title":"Bull","blocks":[{"text":"A bull is an intact adult male of the species Bos taurus (cattle). More muscular and aggressive than the females of the same species, bulls have long been an important symbol in many religions, including for sacrifices. These animals play a significant role in beef ranching, dairy farming, and a variety of sporting and cultural activities, including bullfighting and bull riding."}],"